  "question": {
    "text": "A zener diode with 5 V zener voltage is used to regulate an unregulated dc voltage input of 25 V. For a $400 \\Omega$ resistor connected in series, the zener current is found to be 4 times load current. The load current $\\left(I_L\\right)$ and load resistance $\\left(R_{\\mathrm{L}}\\right)$ are :",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "e78BS",
      "text": "$\\mathrm{I}_{\\mathrm{L}}=20 \\mathrm{~mA} ; \\mathrm{R}_{\\mathrm{L}}=250 \\Omega$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "VGjVc",
      "text": "$\\mathrm{I}_{\\mathrm{L}}=10 \\mathrm{~A} ; \\mathrm{R}_{\\mathrm{L}}=0.5 \\Omega$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "Ov2iu",
      "text": "$\\mathrm{I}_{\\mathrm{L}}=0.02 \\mathrm{~mA} ; \\mathrm{R}_{\\mathrm{L}}=250 \\Omega$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "jIe9L",
      "text": "$\\mathrm{I}_{\\mathrm{L}}=10 \\mathrm{~mA} ; \\mathrm{R}_{\\mathrm{L}}=500 \\Omega$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "<img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/E1DaBwaY9RYop0gfVIxQTMjj9dK_lflcbja14DhX6as.original.fullsize.png\"/><br/>From the circuit diagram,<br/>$\\begin{aligned}<br/>& 5 \\mathrm{i}=\\frac{20}{400}=\\frac{1}{20} \\mathrm{~A} \\\\\n& \\therefore \\mathrm{i}=\\frac{1}{100} \\mathrm{~A}=10 \\mathrm{~mA}=\\text { Load current }<br/>\\end{aligned}$<br/>Also, $\\mathrm{V}_{\\mathrm{L}}=5 \\mathrm{~V}$<br/>$\\therefore \\mathrm{R}_{\\mathrm{L}}=\\frac{5}{10 \\times 10^{-3}} \\Omega=500 \\Omega$",
    "image": null
  },
